<title>NEW ZEALAND: Owens says makes sound start to 1997/98 yr.</title>
<headline>Owens says makes sound start to 1997/98 yr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australasian freight company Owens Group said on Friday it had made a sound start to the new financial year, but predicted that flat New Zealand trading conditions were not likely to improve in calender 1997.</p>
<p>Owens commented, however, that there are some encouraging signs of an upturn in the Australian economy.</p>
<p>Earlier, Ownes reported a flat net profit of NZ$9.14 million, which it described as very satisfactory in the highly competitive markets and flat economic conditions in New Zealand and Australia.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
